**Bug found and fixed.**

In `src/sim.ts` line 43, the condition was `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` — meaning population grew even when production exactly equaled consumption (zero surplus). This caused settlements to keep growing indefinitely as long as they weren't losing food.

**Fix:** Changed `>=` to `>` so population only grows when there's an actual surplus (food produced > food consumed).

**Verified:** All 4 tests pass, typecheck passes.


